# SRE Configuration

> **How to use:**
> 1. Copy this file to `sre-config.md` in the same directory.
> 2. Fill in every value marked `{fill in}` with your team's actual values.
> 3. `sre-config.md` is gitignored — your real values stay local and never get committed.
> 4. The SRE skills read `sre-config.md` at the start of every run.
>    If `sre-config.md` is missing, skills fall back to this file and warn you.

---

## Atlassian / Jira

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| Jira project key | `YOUR_PROJECT` |
| Jira cloud ID | `{fill in — from your Atlassian admin panel or API}` |
| Jira base URL | `https://your-org.atlassian.net` |
| Confluence space key | `YOUR_SPACE` |

## Slack (optional)

> Remove this section if you are not using the Slack MCP integration.
> Without Slack configured, the skills save notifications to `output/alerts/` instead.

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| Internal SRE channel ID | `C0XXXXXXXXX` |
| Team / announce channel ID | `C0XXXXXXXXX` |

## AWS Infrastructure

| Key | Value |
|---|---|
| AWS account ID | `{fill in}` |
| Primary region | `us-east-1` |
| ECR prefix | `{account-id}.dkr.ecr.{region}.amazonaws.com/` |
| Secret naming pattern | `eks-{cluster-prefix}-{app-name}` |

